 "text": "A 66 acre park on the Arkansas River in Tulsa, five acres of playgrounds, a boathouse, a skate park, trails, and big open lawns, more than 6,000 trees, and admission is free. It was built with the largest private gift to a community park in U.S. history. In 2024, USA Today readers named it the best city park in America. Have a slow Sunday.",
